// Generated by build/drills.py from the club's old drill pages.
const CLUB_DRILLS = [{"id": "100-throws", "title": "100 Throws", "players": "2", "cat": "Fundamentals", "tags": ["Throwing", "Catching", "Pivots & fakes", "Warm-up"], "summary": "Pairs, 50 backhands and 50 forehands, every throw to the chest with a fake and pivot first.", "thumb": null, "html": "<></>\n<p>It is simply to pair up and make 50 backhand and 50 sidearm throws to each other over 5-10m (changing ends after 50 if windy). The most important thing to get value from this drill is the way in which you do it!</p>\n<p>Every throw should be hitting the other persons chest – accuracy!</p>\n<p>Every catch should be attacked like you were in a game and taken with 2 hands.</p>\n<p>Every throw should be done with a good balanced body position as described in the throwing techniques section.</p>\n<p>Every throw should be proceeded with a good fake and a pivot.</p>\n<p>Vary the height of release and the shape of the flight as you go through the 100.</p>\n<p>If you make an error on a certain throw repeat it 3 times correctly before changing to another. This is hard work you should be hot and mentally tired by this throwing drill when done correctly.</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "super-70s", "title": "Super 70s", "players": "2", "cat": "Fundamentals", "tags": ["Throwing", "Catching", "Warm-up"], "summary": "A shorter, indoor-friendly 100 throws: 10 each of seven throws, with press-ups for errors.", "thumb": null, "html": "<></>\n<p>This is a shorter version of the 100 throws which is more suited to indoor Ultimate Frisbee drills.</p>\n<p>10 Roll curve backhand</p>\n<p>10 Straight backhand</p>\n<p>10 ‘I.O’ or skip curve</p>\n<p>10 Roll curve</p>\n<p>10 Straight forehand</p>\n<p>10 ‘I.O’ or skip curve forehand</p>\n<p>10 Hammer</p>\n<p>Again over 5m-10m, this time each drop or throw away is counted by the pair then multiplied by the years they’ve been playing ultimate for some form of punishment!</p>\n<p>For example: Cap &amp; Chelsea do super 70’s. there is 1 drop and 1 thrown away = 2 errors.</p>\n<p>Cap 12 years playing Ultimate makes 2 errors = 24 push ups / Chelsea 4 years playing makes 2 errors = 8 push ups</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "pivot-drill", "title": "Pivot Drill", "players": "4–6", "cat": "Fundamentals", "tags": ["Pivots & fakes", "Throwing"], "summary": "A player in the middle of a square receives, pivots and passes, building footwork and body position.", "thumb": "img/4b7bb5466151e1124697052925746d27.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4b7bb5466151e1124697052925746d27.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>This drill should be done in groups of 4,5 or 6 with 2 less discs than players.</p>\n<p>The player in the centre of the square receives a pass from one corner and then pivots to face a player without a disc and passes to them. Then they pivot to face another player with a disc to receive a pass from them. Then pivot again to make a pass to the player without a disc.</p>\n<p>Important things:</p>\n<p>Maintain eye contact</p>\n<p>Correct footwork</p>\n<p>Good body position to make each throw</p>\n<p>Change direction of the pivots (i.e. rotate both clockwise and anti-clockwise)</p>\n<p>Challenge the players to pivot as slowly and far as possible with good form, then gradually speed it up. Each player has 3 minutes in the middle then switches.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "break-force", "title": "Break Force Drill", "players": "3", "cat": "Fundamentals", "tags": ["Breaking the mark", "Marking", "Pivots & fakes", "Warm-up"], "summary": "Piggy in the middle with a straight-up mark: fake, pivot and beat the mark, then follow your throw to mark.", "thumb": null, "html": "<></>\n<p>A simple 3 player Ultimate Frisbee drill, based on piggy in the middle.</p>\n<p>The player with the disc has a ‘straight up’ force (mark) on them.</p>\n<p>They have to throw to the other person (approx 10m away) by faking and pivoting to beat the mark.</p>\n<p>Once the pass is made, the thrower follows the pass to put a mark on the receiver.</p>\n<p>The player with the disc then has to beat the mark to throw to the other person, and so on.</p>\n<p>This is a good warm up to play before a game as it involves playing the 3 main skills in Ultimate: passing, receiving and marking.</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "pivot-n-fake", "title": "Pivot'n'Fake", "players": "2", "cat": "Fundamentals", "tags": ["Pivots & fakes", "Throwing"], "summary": "Partner raises a hand mid-throw; you pump fake, pivot and throw the other side.", "thumb": null, "html": "<></>\n<p>The objective of this is to work on the fundamental principles of throwing, faking and pivoting. Pair up and use a single disc.</p>\n<p>Stand ~10m apart start by looking 'upfield' then pivot to turn and look at your partner who should be stood in the swing position. start to throw either a backhand or forehand to them (Remember to pivot properly!).</p>\n<p>If you partner puts their hand up at any point before the disc has left your hand pump fake the throw, pivot and throw the alternative option.</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "break-throwing", "title": "Break Throwing (with and without a defender)", "players": "3+", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Breaking the mark", "Throwing", "Decision making"], "summary": "Start with the Centurion, then practise inside and around breaks, first unmarked and then with an active defender.", "thumb": "img/255a3ae3efe8b3702e88f1101685020a.webp", "html": "<div class=\"video\" data-yt=\"AOiyhY8oJno\"></div>\n<></>\n<p>Follow the Centurion, then go in to the next drill utilising the appropriate throws</p>\n<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/255a3ae3efe8b3702e88f1101685020a.webp\"/></figure><div><h3>Break throwing V1 (No Defender)</h3>\n<p>With the first drill its mostly about just throwing the break, ideally we want the inside  break but with an around rather than a low release, for the second people need to think more, so if the defender is too tight on the inside on the backhand then pivot around for the flick in to space so its not just about the technical throw its about thinking where is the defender and \"what is the best thing I can throw\"?</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/677d659ca2fb000994a74787b1f16e92.webp\"/></figure><div><h3>Break throwing V2 (With Defender)</h3>\n<p>with the second version with the defenders the offence cutter runs out the line, slaps hands with the defenders then the defender can activate.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "box-drill", "title": "Box Drill", "players": "8+", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Throwing", "Timing", "Communication", "Warm-up"], "summary": "This drill is about 3 things. Throwing accuracy in different directions (assuming wind), timing of cuts & communication. The cut should be underway before th…", "thumb": "img/d0e3b7b1848e9c7ef53cc4082e46072f.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/d0e3b7b1848e9c7ef53cc4082e46072f.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>This drill is about 3 things. Throwing accuracy in different directions (assuming wind), timing of cuts &amp; communication. The cut should be underway before the thrower has caught the disc.</p>\n<p>The cutter should call for the disc.</p>\n<p>Things to be careful with - where you cut. Avoid running into the cutter before you if your both running to the centre of the square. Queuing people need to be heads up if the disc is coming towards them.</p>\n<p>Change direction after 4-8 loops perhaps.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "swiss-drill", "title": "Swiss Drill", "players": "8+", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Throwing", "Timing", "Warm-up"], "summary": "Swiss Drill. Similar to the box drill in that it encourages you to throw in different directions & timings of cuts need to be good. I would encourage players…", "thumb": "img/ee6bddcd5d795b3687fac79bbbd1251c.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/ee6bddcd5d795b3687fac79bbbd1251c.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>Swiss Drill. Similar to the box drill in that it encourages you to throw in different directions &amp; timings of cuts need to be good. I would encourage players to call for the disc when they turn in the cut.</p>\n<p>If you have enough players you can run 2 Swiss drills back to back so you can practice backhand and forehand in both directions.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/8538f34920062018879120cdeb28ae76.webp\"/></figure><div><h3>Swiss Drill (Variation)</h3>\n<p>Always clear out back into the middle. Avoid collisions &amp; encourage players to cut from all 4 cones.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "lead-passes", "title": "Lead Passes (and with a fake)", "players": "4+", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Lead pass", "Throwing", "Timing"], "summary": "Two queues; throw a curved lead pass in front of a cutter running out of the stack, then add a fake from the cutter.", "thumb": "img/d65ef2be35f27915840a769c7c12eea7.webp", "html": "<></>\n<div class=\"steps\"><div class=\"step\"><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/d65ef2be35f27915840a769c7c12eea7.webp\"/><div class=\"body\"><h4>Standard Lead Pass</h4><p>This drill is pretty much all about the throw. It is likely to have a role on to make it easier to catch &amp; it and should be in front of the receiver.</p>\n<p>2 cones 7-10m apart (?) and off set by 5m (see diagram). 2 queues on cones. Thrower starts with disc in the drill (as if s/he has just caught the disc.</p>\n<p>Cutter runs straight out of stack. Disc thrown to arrive in front of receiver. Receiver then pivots, gets balance and throws lovely role curved disc to next cutter.</p>\n<p>Things to consider - after catching, properly take time to pivot and get balance, role curve the disc outside in. Throw for your cutter. Are they fast? Are they a bit slower?</p></div></div><div class=\"step\"><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/72fac216c61ee944ed76286de47ce59a.webp\"/><div class=\"body\"><h4>Lead Pass with Fake</h4><p>This can also be augmented to encourage a fake from the cutter.</p></div></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "diagonal-lead-passes", "title": "Diagonal Lead Passes", "players": "6+", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Lead pass", "Breaking the mark", "Timing"], "summary": "2 queues of people cuts to either open or break side.", "thumb": "img/2921204e426bf59c8c2b0d79457a73d4.webp", "html": "<></>\n<p>2 queues of people cuts to either open or break side.</p>\n<p>Break side throws can be flow &amp; flat or high arcing = banked (outside in)</p>\n<div class=\"steps\"><div class=\"step\"><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2921204e426bf59c8c2b0d79457a73d4.webp\"/><div class=\"body\"><p>Player 2 throws a lead pass to P1 (cutter), who then joins the back of the opposite P2 throwing queue. Continue flow with a throw to the last in queue/goal. The thrower becomes the next cutter</p></div></div><div class=\"step\"><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/f82bccf704dbbc5a6152238e7be4400b.webp\"/><div class=\"body\"><p>Dump handler retreats then cuts upfield on the break side and receives break throw lead pass. The thrower becomes the dump. Flow can be continued by passing to the back of the queue after the catch.</p></div></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "x-drill", "title": "X Drill (DED Warm-up)", "players": "6+", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Timing", "Lead pass", "Warm-up"], "summary": "The objective of this drill is to focus on the timing of cuts and throws. We set up two stacks ~10m apart only using a single disc. LHS queue cuts diagonally…", "thumb": "img/2f7a4aa61f4b4e8f6d272b022a827065.webp", "html": "<></>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2f7a4aa61f4b4e8f6d272b022a827065.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>The objective of this drill is to focus on the timing of cuts and throws. We set up two stacks ~10m apart only using a single disc. LHS queue cuts diagonally up line and RHS disc is thrown just in front. Immediately after throwing RHS front of stack cuts diagonally to the opposite side to receive a swing leading pass. On receipt dump to the front of the stack and join the back of the queue</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "line-break-active-force", "title": "Line Break Throws with an Active Force", "players": "3+", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Breaking the mark", "Pivots & fakes", "Lead pass"], "summary": "Fake to turn the cutter, then break the force with a leading pass; swap roles each rep.", "thumb": "img/1e1e13d68a978abc617379a9544a5a92.webp", "html": "<></>\n<h3>Line Break Throws W/Active Force</h3>\n<div class=\"steps\"><div class=\"step\"><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/1e1e13d68a978abc617379a9544a5a92.webp\"/><div class=\"body\"><h4>Step 1</h4><p>One player starts with the disc with a force. Opposing cutter sprints to the near cone. the thrower then throws a fake which causes the cutter to turn then sprint to the opposite cone. Player on disc then throws a break throw for a leading pass.</p></div></div><div class=\"step\"><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/d038c27cf2811434aef4d1b3e558ad5e.webp\"/><div class=\"body\"><h4>Step 2</h4><p>After throwing the player then cuts to the opposite cone, the cutter who originally received throws a fake causing the 'handler' to cut backwards to receive a leading pass. The cycle then repeats but force/thrower swap.</p></div></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "wipers", "title": "Wipers", "players": "3", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Catching", "Throwing"], "summary": "A receiver swings between two cones catching on both sides while a thrower alternates backhands and forehands.", "thumb": "img/01a88679eb004258aaa288863f05754a.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/01a88679eb004258aaa288863f05754a.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>Number of people: 3</p>\n<p>Short Info: catcher runs back and forth between two cones. Stationary marker.</p>\n<p>Long: Picture a triangle, 10 feet on a side. Cones are on two corners, a thrower and marker on the other corner. Receiver swings back and forth between the two cones, catching a throw near one cone, throwing it back, running to the other cone, catching and throwing it back, repeating this for a couple of minutes. To make this go smoothly, the marker shouldn't mark hard at all. In fact, he should just stand still, crouched down slightly, with arms out.</p>\n<p>Strengths: Receiver has to stretch to both sides for catches, so the drill works on quick right and left-handed catches. Thrower has to quickly throw both forehands and backhands.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "continuations-to-huck", "title": "Continuations to Huck", "players": "6+", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Hucking", "Continuations", "Timing"], "summary": "The focus of this drill is continuations and short throws with touch leading to a long huck. We set up in two stacks of equal size, a thrower with a disc on …", "thumb": "img/f9847f023fd3606b97641441a0e62215.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/f9847f023fd3606b97641441a0e62215.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>The focus of this drill is continuations and short throws with touch leading to a long huck. We set up in two stacks of equal size, a thrower with a disc on one side and cutters on cones on the other. 1st cutter cuts under then up the line to the cone diagonally opposite to receive a leading pass, they then pass to the next cutter who is cutting up the line for the continuation and so on until you get to the 2nd from last cutter.</p>\n<p>Prior to this the end of the cutters should have started to sprint long looking for the long put from a power position. If the end cutter does not have the throw then please call the long shot under to ensure the completion of the pass.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "intelligent-hucking", "title": "Intelligent Hucking", "players": "4+", "cat": "Throwing", "tags": ["Hucking", "Decision making", "Match defence"], "summary": "Pick the right huck for the force and the defender: target the space while a defender in a \"funnel\" tries to block.", "thumb": "img/01d86a67c99e7d8f1e5dbfe9611d5879.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/01d86a67c99e7d8f1e5dbfe9611d5879.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>There are two active pairs at any time during this drill (you can run two drills at once with the funnel structure).</p>\n<p>A/C are the offensive pair, B/D are the defensive pair.  B  throws a pop pass to A and then immediately runs to put a force on. the moment that the disc is received A looks for the huck long. The objective of the drill is to consider the best throw for the situation to end up in the 'Target' space. Assume a right handed thrower for the top iteration it would be a Outside-In backhand.  if the disc enters the 'funnel' then it is considered to be a block by defensive player 'D'. There are several iterations of this drill given below:</p></div></div>\n<p>The first iteration of the drill is for the upper side you are looking to use a flat or OI backhand in to the target space keeping the receiver between the defender and the disc, in this 1st set the defender cannot move beyond the limits of the funnel in to the pitch 'proper'. For the lower drill it would be an outside flick in to the target space.</p>\n<p>The same as the upper but now the moment the disc leaves the throwers hand (for the long not the pop) the defender can move in to the pitch 'proper' and make a bid on the disc.</p>\n<p>switch the forces and the defender is once again constrained to the funnel, the shot for the top would now become an OI flick and for the lower half it would become an OI backhand</p>\n<p>same as step 3 but the defender is now allowed to move out of the funnel in to the pitch to bid on the disc</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "under-cuts", "title": "Under Cuts", "players": "4+", "cat": "Cutting", "tags": ["Cutting", "Lead pass", "Pivots & fakes"], "summary": "Two stacks. First side cuts up, thrower fakes and shouts \"nope\".", "thumb": "img/285d66d038f2d91bd44cafaad486102c.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/285d66d038f2d91bd44cafaad486102c.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>Two stacks. First side cuts up, thrower fakes and shouts \"nope\".</p>\n<p>Cutter does a sharp turn and comes under for an up line leading pass to the chest.</p>\n<p>Thrower then cuts upfield. We want a light outwards force on the thrower to make the throw more difficult but no a very active.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "three-player-weave", "title": "3 Player Weave", "players": "3", "cat": "Cutting", "tags": ["Cutting", "Lead pass", "Throwing", "Warm-up"], "summary": "Inside-out lead passes on the run: follow your throw across and keep weaving up the pitch.", "thumb": "img/e5c53fb6a3f5d8c0b49d679ee070560e.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/e5c53fb6a3f5d8c0b49d679ee070560e.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>Throws to the RHS are forehand (or lefty backhand) &amp; throws to your LHS are backhand.</p>\n<p>Follow your throw to the other side of the pitch and continue to run straight on that side until you receive the disc back from the player that was previously behind you.</p>\n<p>Throw again to the player you first threw to, but this time from the opposite side. Change side and receive the disc, again from the same player that previously threw it to you.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "attack-the-under", "title": "Defensive Run, Attack the Disc, Give-and-Go", "players": "2+", "cat": "Cutting", "tags": ["Footwork", "Cutting", "Catching"], "summary": "Backpedal, shuffle, sprint, then plant and attack an under cut, throw and go for the return.", "thumb": "img/c109e6f5aa6e6c7980309fb83f9c7daa.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/c109e6f5aa6e6c7980309fb83f9c7daa.webp\"/></figure><div><h3>Defensive Run + Attacking the Disc for 'interception' on an Under Cut + Give and Go</h3>\n<p>Player 1 Backpedals (3s), Side Steps --&gt; crossovers (3s), Normal Sprint (3s), Hard Stop &amp; Cut Back Under @ 45 Degrees (Attack) to get the disc &amp; throw back to advancing P2. P1 then cuts behind P2 back towards the starting cone and receives a short leading pass. P2 then backpedals...</p>\n<p>Each Player cuts twice for cross over sprints facing both sides.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "ho-diamonds-pistons", "title": "Horizontal Stack Diamonds & Pistons", "players": "7", "cat": "Cutting", "tags": ["Ho stack", "Cutting", "Continuations"], "summary": "Two horizontal-stack cutting continuations: diamonds and pistons.", "thumb": "img/189087970d8b39cd3a2f42855a6d74fe.webp", "html": "<div class=\"steps\"><div class=\"step\"><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/189087970d8b39cd3a2f42855a6d74fe.webp\"/><div class=\"body\"></div></div><div class=\"step\"><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/908c4ff721567413e83ffd2b65144104.webp\"/><div class=\"body\"><h4>Horizontal Stack 'Pistons' Cutting Continuation</h4></div></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "hillman", "title": "Hillman Drill", "players": "4", "cat": "Cutting", "tags": ["Getting open", "Match defence", "Positioning"], "summary": "The objective of this drill is simple, get free and receive the disc in two cuts or less. A/C on defence, B/D on offence. The goal of 'C' is to use their bod…", "thumb": "img/0ae12a052ac64fd07ef4f67b61406df0.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/0ae12a052ac64fd07ef4f67b61406df0.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>The objective of this drill is simple, get free and receive the disc in two cuts or less. A/C on defence, B/D on offence. The goal of 'C' is to use their body to dictate where 'D' can cut to on pitch. Offence can set up anywhere in the white square but the whole pitch is in play for the 'threat space'.</p>\n<p>For defence, remember the ideals of tight, chest-to-chest defence. Tight D wins games: take the hit of them trying to run through you. The deep threat is not the biggest concern, stop unders to the open side at all cost  :)</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "upline-break-cuts", "title": "Up-line Break Cuts and Throws", "players": "3+", "cat": "Cutting", "tags": ["Handler resets", "Breaking the mark", "Cutting"], "summary": "Diagram sequence for up-line break cuts and the throws that hit them.", "thumb": "img/d00789965c1374054147549fe5038b9d.webp", "html": "<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/d00789965c1374054147549fe5038b9d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/1c9ebe950265a0cd08b52f3565aa0b67.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/cc33200ceaf60a89dcea814823e6f7a1.webp\"/></figure>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "upline-slash-deep", "title": "Up Line, Slash, Deep", "players": "3+", "cat": "Cutting", "tags": ["Cutting", "Continuations", "Timing"], "summary": "Diagram sequence linking an up-line cut, a slash and a deep shot.", "thumb": "img/b84008a82e3d7ed02d569ebfb7619fb4.webp", "html": "<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/b84008a82e3d7ed02d569ebfb7619fb4.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/d3d5b417286555aaf383f8947a2b6cec.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/c726a523176e3d7a5491bfb87bd71fd1.webp\"/></figure>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "phases-horizontal", "title": "Phases of Play: Horizontal (Advanced)", "players": "7", "cat": "Team play", "tags": ["Ho stack", "Handler resets", "Continuations", "Team cutting patterns"], "summary": "Phase 0 to Phase 3 of our horizontal offence, from the up-line handler cut to the reset.", "thumb": "img/d229b7f896f03b01d9980ea88484c0ea.webp", "html": "<></>\n<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/d229b7f896f03b01d9980ea88484c0ea.webp\"/></figure><div><h3>Phase 0</h3>\n<p>Here we have Phase 0, in this instance the dump handler has cut up the line and received a pass from the current handler on disc, this then moves us in to phase 1.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/609c0758fa068e96e5a218bfc941aefb.webp\"/></figure><div><h3>Phase 1a</h3>\n<p>In phase 1 once the disc has been thrown to the up line cut handler the now reset handler pushes up in to the reset space</p>\n<p>the cutter in line with the handler strikes deep for a long shot, while the middle pair stays still, if the deep shot isn't on then the handler throws a fake and PHASE 2 begins.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/b02da2fd659a30cb0ace5594892bdccb.webp\"/></figure><div><h3>Phase 1b</h3>\n<p>In phase 1 once the disc has been thrown to the up line cut handler the now reset handler pushes up in to the reset space.</p>\n<p>At the same time the cutter in line with the new handlers cut deep strait away while the middle cutter makes a slash cut across pitch to provide an option for the handler. In this instance we jump strait from PHASE 1 to PHASE 3</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/c2c3b9fc9414cf21259964023098d30a.webp\"/></figure><div><h3>Phase 2</h3>\n<p>For phase 2 the middle cutter who has not yet been engaged does a slash cut across pitch to get the disc providing an option for the handler as the cutter who cut deep now cuts diagonally in to the under space to provide a new option.</p></div></div>\n<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6f1933f71cfc2936801b22384c8b851a.webp\"/></figure><div><h3>Phase 3</h3>\n<p>Phase 3 is when we look for our reset, at this point it is the job of the new dump handler to get free either by cutting up the line or faking an up the line and going for a reset back and the process starts again</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "mushroom", "title": "Mushroom", "players": "6+", "cat": "Endzone", "tags": ["Endzone", "Handler resets", "Lead pass"], "summary": "One line in the endzone: juke cuts to the thrower, then dump and swing cuts back and forth.", "thumb": "img/2cfa5fb39df4a8bee9919ed7a29d543c.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2cfa5fb39df4a8bee9919ed7a29d543c.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>Purpose: To practice dumping and swinging and throwing to a moving receiver.</p>\n<p>Number of Players: 6+</p>\n<p>Number of discs: 1</p>\n<ul><li>Set up one line in the front middle of the endzone (Fig 23a)</li><li>A starts with the disc 10 yards away from the front of the line (Fig 23a)</li><li>B makes a two step juke cut to the forehand side (Fig 23b)</li><li>A throws a forehand to B (Fig 23b)</li><li>C makes a two step juke cut to continue the pass (Fig 23c)</li><li>Once a player catches a disc in the endzone the next cut is a dump cut in the opposite direction (Fig 23d)</li><li>Continue back and forth</li></ul></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "seattle", "title": "Seattle Drill", "players": "7+", "cat": "Endzone", "tags": ["Endzone", "Handler resets", "Lead pass"], "summary": "Purpose: To practice endzone offense, dumping and swinging, endzone cuts, and throwing to a moving receiver.", "thumb": "img/d62f06c376579465e9ef7fd272cb378f.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/d62f06c376579465e9ef7fd272cb378f.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>Purpose: To practice endzone offense, dumping and swinging, endzone cuts, and throwing to a moving receiver.</p>\n<p>Number of Players: 7+</p>\n<p>Number of Discs: 1</p>\n<p>Description:</p>\n<ul><li>Set up two lines – one in the front middle of the endzone, the other in the back middle. (Fig. 24a)</li><li>A1 starts with the disc 10 yards away from line A (Fig. 24a)</li><li>A2 makes a two step juke cut to the forehand side (Fig. 24b)</li><li>A1 throws a forehand to A2 (Fig. 24b)</li><li>B1 makes a full cut or a straight cut toward the front corner of the endzone (Fig. 24 c)</li><li>A2 throws a forehand to B1 (Fig. 24c)</li><li>A3 makes a dump cut for B1 (Fig. 24d)</li><li>B1 throws a backhand dump to A3 (Fig. 24d)</li><li>Continue scoring in each corner</li><li>After catching a score recycle into line A</li><li>After throwing a score recycle into line B</li><li>After catching a dump pass, recycle into line A (otherwise the lines will get uneven)</li></ul></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "d-circle", "title": "D Circle", "players": "8+", "cat": "Defence", "tags": ["Zone defence", "Marking", "Pivots & fakes"], "summary": "A three-person cup contains a thrower inside a circle of receivers; fake and pivot to beat it.", "thumb": "img/c4187285b2c395dbc67c321a56974f4f.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/c4187285b2c395dbc67c321a56974f4f.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>Purpose: To practice containing in the cup (zone D), faking and pivoting.</p>\n<p>Number of Discs: 1</p>\n<p>Description: - All but three players form a circle with a diameter of 25 yards (Fig. 25a)</p>\n<ul><li>The three defensive players set up a cup around the player with the disc (Fig. 25a)</li></ul>\n<p>o One point should be forcing to the other point and stalling – initiating the stall count at “stalling \t4”</p>\n<p>o The Middle-middle should be stopping throws through the cup</p>\n<ul><li>The thrower must fake and pivot in order to throw to another player in the circle (Fig. 25b)</li><li>The thrower can not throw to the receivers immediately on his right or left</li><li>Once the thrower throws, the cup moves to set up on the new thrower</li><li>The first defensive player should set up a mark that stops the continuation pass and forces the disc back to the other defensive players (Fig. 25c)</li><li>If there is an incomplete pass – the defense gets to set up and initiate play with a check</li><li>Continue for a set time or to a specific number of blocks and then rotate the defense out</li></ul></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "defensive-positioning", "title": "Defensive Positioning", "players": "4+", "cat": "Defence", "tags": ["Match defence", "Positioning", "Getting open"], "summary": "Declare which way you are forcing the receiver, then cover whatever cut they make.", "thumb": "img/e73942d0af2d2a65c46de2fedfb612ee.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/e73942d0af2d2a65c46de2fedfb612ee.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>Purpose: To practice defensive positioning, cutting, and catching while being defended.</p>\n<p>Number of Discs: 3+</p>\n<p>Description:</p>\n<ul><li>The thrower starts with all the discs within 1 yard of the sideline (Fig. 26a)</li><li>The marker forces the thrower towards the sideline (Fig 26a)</li><li>There is a line of defenders 10 yards across and 15 yards downfield of the thrower (Fig. 26a)</li><li>There is a line of receivers 2 yards downfield of the defender line (Fig. 26a)</li><li>The first receiver steps out from the line (Fig. 26b)</li><li>The first defensive players sets up in a position to force the receiver either – deep or back to the disc and announces which way he’s forcing the receiver to go (Fig. 26b)</li><li>The thrower checks the disc in</li><li>The receiver makes any kind of cut in whatever direction she wants trying to get open (Fig. 26c or 26e)</li><li>The defender tries to cover the cut</li><li>The thrower throws to the receiver</li><li>The receiver brings the disc back to the thrower (Fig. 26)</li><li>The receiver and the defender switch lines</li><li>Every player is the thrower for five passes</li></ul></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "positioning-triangle", "title": "Defensive Positioning Triangle", "players": "1+", "cat": "Defence", "tags": ["Positioning", "Footwork", "Match defence"], "summary": "This drill works on defensive positioning for various cuts. For this you're going to do a break cut, deep cut and an under cut. The focus being on how to tur…", "thumb": "img/de4f1f7eaafb14c6a90a6dc07e79e4ce.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/de4f1f7eaafb14c6a90a6dc07e79e4ce.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>This drill works on defensive positioning for various cuts. For this you're going to do a break cut, deep cut and an under cut. The focus being on how to turn your hips and how to position yourself at all stages of the 'triangle'.</p>\n<p>set up 3 cones in a triangle with about 10 yards between cones.</p>\n<p>Start on the left hand cone (break side) and assume a forehand force on the thrower.</p>\n<p>Make a deep cut, plant at the far cone and come under plant at the near cone then act like you would be clearing to the break side. Make sure to keep eye contact with the thrower as you clear as that is a viable option!</p>\n<p>when you get to the cone on the far left sprint deep for a long forehand put.</p>\n<p>Things to focus on. Defence always stay on the open side as shown by the yellow circle.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "open-side-unders", "title": "Defending Open Side Unders", "players": "2", "cat": "Defence", "tags": ["Match defence", "Positioning"], "summary": "A gate race: beat the cutter to the open-side under gate, or match them to the deep gate.", "thumb": "img/7a855ec42312d1e8d15279033b3adac7.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/7a855ec42312d1e8d15279033b3adac7.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>No discs are needed for this drill, the importance is the taking away of the open side under yet still being close enough to bid in the event that a long throw is used.</p>\n<p>set up a rectangle as shown in the diagram. LHS corresponds to the deep space, RHS the open side under.</p>\n<p>Set up in a defender/attacker position. The objective is that if the offence gets through the Open Under \"gate\" before the defence the defender has lost and has to do 10 press-ups.</p>\n<p>If the offence runs to the deep space the defender must get through the first gate before or at the same time as the offence gets through the further deep gate else defender does 10 pushups.</p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "hockey-stop", "title": "Crossover Hockey Stop", "players": "1", "cat": "Agility", "tags": ["Footwork", "Agility"], "summary": "Learn the low, wide hockey stop position, then practise it with lateral momentum.", "thumb": null, "html": "<div class=\"video\" data-yt=\"-QIQe2_Rr_s\"></div>\n<></>\n<p>In order to push the body in any direction, the feet must be outside the center of mass. To change direction laterally or at a sharp angle, your body ends up in what we call the hockey stop position.</p>\n<p>This hockey stop position places the outside leg far outside of the center of mass and allows the center of mass to get low while you decelerate and accelerate in the opposite direction.</p>\n<p>The center of mass remains closer to the inside leg. The outside leg absorbs a lot of lateral force and should be bent at a 10-20 degree angle.</p>\n<div class=\"video\" data-yt=\"JY-mgxRhqlU\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 1 - Crossover Hockey Stop</h3>\n<p>This drill works on getting comfortable in the position with a bit of lateral momentum</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "short-slalom", "title": "Short Slalom", "players": "1", "cat": "Agility", "tags": ["Footwork", "Agility"], "summary": "The short slalom drill challenges you to get lower than is comfortable and helps you get your feet far out of your center of mass. You'll know you're doing t…", "thumb": null, "html": "<div class=\"video\" data-yt=\"Uc76LkiIDNY\"></div>\n<></>\n<p>The short slalom drill challenges you to get lower than is comfortable and helps you get your feet far out of your center of mass. You’ll know you’re doing this drill correctly if you occasionally feel off balance or sometimes even hit the dirt.</p>\n<p>You’re trying to push the edge of your comfort zone and that means failing every now and then.</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "five-ten", "title": "5–10 Drill", "players": "1", "cat": "Agility", "tags": ["Footwork", "Agility", "Match defence"], "summary": "This drill helps to brings awareness to your hips. On defense you want to keep your hips open toward the person you're covering as much as possible. On offen…", "thumb": null, "html": "<div class=\"video\" data-yt=\"LG3SkWKKLHk\"></div>\n<></>\n<p>This drill helps to brings awareness to your hips. On defense you want to keep your hips open toward the person you’re covering as much as possible. On offense, keeping your hips open on short cuts will help you to fake and cut more quickly.</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "quarter-turn", "title": "2 Steps to Quarter Turn", "players": "1", "cat": "Agility", "tags": ["Footwork", "Agility"], "summary": "For efficient change of direction you need to open your hips. This drill explores the feeling of foot placement and hip opening into the turn. Notice Will's …", "thumb": null, "html": "<div class=\"video\" data-yt=\"Yrvtw73t1bw\"></div>\n<></>\n<p>For efficient change of direction you need to open your hips. This drill explores the feeling of foot placement and hip opening into the turn. Notice Will’s foot angle in the step before the plant. The right foot toe starts pointing towards the camera instead of directly at the line. Where the toes go the hips follow. This foot placement is what we’re talking about when we are opening the hips.</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "shuffle-cone-touch", "title": "Short Shuffle with Cone Touch", "players": "1", "cat": "Agility", "tags": ["Footwork", "Agility"], "summary": "In the drill below, the focus is on both form and speed. Touch the cone with the inside hand and allow the feet to get outside the center of mass (beyond the…", "thumb": null, "html": "<div class=\"video\" data-yt=\"5di130Hlpos\"></div>\n<></>\n<p>In the drill below, the focus is on both form and speed. Touch the cone with the inside hand and allow the feet to get outside the center of mass (beyond the cones.</p>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "agility-cones", "title": "Agility Cones", "players": "1", "cat": "Agility", "tags": ["Footwork", "Agility", "Conditioning"], "summary": "This workout is designed to increase your quickness, improve your footwork, and generally make you more explosive and agile.", "thumb": "img/6c87d64640eb01058fa5b126f6e17a28.webp", "html": "<div class=\"split\"><figure><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6c87d64640eb01058fa5b126f6e17a28.webp\"/></figure><div>\n<p>This workout is designed to increase your quickness, improve your footwork, and generally make you more explosive and agile.</p>\n<p>After your warmup, set up your cones to make use of the full space available to you by dropping the first at one end of your available space and another about 20 yards away. Then, fill in the space between with your remaining cones in a serpentine pattern, walking each cone about five yards away in a diagonal opposite direction from the last one. As easy as that, you have created a small agility course.</p>\n<p>Running the course (ideally with cleats on grass or turf) can work on a variety of things such as planting and changing direction, exploding out of a jab step, keeping your feet and hips under you, and can improve your quickness and fitness.</p>\n<p>Routines:</p>\n<p>Sprint forward through the course with a quick lateral change of direction around each cone</p>\n<p>Shuffle sideways through the course with a quick lateral change of direction around each cone</p>\n<p>Backpedal through the course with a quick lateral change of direction around each cone</p>\n<p>Backpedal around a cone, then forward explosion sprint to the next cone, always facing the same direction</p>\n<p>More variations of this can be found here:</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://kingsportstraining.com/8269753-10-best-speed-and-agility-cone-drills\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">https://kingsportstraining.com/8269753-10-best-speed-and-agility-cone-drills</a></p></div></div>", "source": "club"}, {"id": "defensive-footwork", "title": "Defensive Footwork Gauntlet (10 drills)", "players": "1", "cat": "Agility", "tags": ["Footwork", "Match defence", "Agility"], "summary": "Ten progressive footwork patterns for defenders (slides, falling leaf, Hollywood squares and more), each with a video.", "thumb": null, "html": "<></>\n<p>Please note:</p>\n<p>You will get  benefit from working a few patterns a day, but if you're really focusing on defense we suggest doing a short gauntlet of these drills in the order presented. Each one of these builds on the foundation of the other - the core stiffness you gain from doing the Slaloms translates into snappier 2-In-2-Outs, which preps you to put your feet down in the places you need to for the Jab/Crossover, which lowers your weight for a better transition to sprint/reactive drills. Twice through 2-3 patterns in each section is a strong piece of your track workout.</p>\n<p>HOWEVER:</p>\n<p>If you start feeling pain in your inner thigh or knee area please stop IMMEDIATELY. Slaloms or any other side-to-side exercises may lead to a stressed out groin ligament or one of your adductors</p>\n<p>In the event your movement gets at all sluggish (as it might with that many reps) you were probably putting too much stress on your connective tissue by spending a little too much time on the ground. Make sure you also recover fully in between sets Take a few minutes between drills to rest and set up the next drill.</p>\n<p>Warm up</p>\n<p>Recommend ~15 minutes—something to get heart rate up (throw, jog, bike, light agility ladder) and movements/exercises that will:</p>\n<p>mobilize your hips, ankles, shoulders and t-spine</p>\n<p>activate your core and glutes</p>\n<p>2 reps of slide progression</p>\n<p>One rep starting left, the other rep starting right</p>\n<p>90s between reps</p>\n<p>2 sets of 4 reps of focused falling leaf</p>\n<p>One set slide, the other set crossover run</p>\n<p>15s between reps (enough time to walk back to the starting point)</p>\n<p>90s between sets</p>\n<p>4 sets of 2 reps of jumbo hollywood squares</p>\n<p>For each set, one rep force backhand, the other rep force flick</p>\n<p>15s between reps (enough time to walk to the starting point)</p>\n<p>90s between sets</p>\n<p>Once you get the hang of this consider finishing each rep by either chopping down to defend a second underneath cut or finding and chasing down an imaginary huck</p>\n<p>A few more things:</p>\n<p>If you’re an experienced defender and find these basic, consider:</p>\n<p>Pushing the precision and speed of your footwork to new levels</p>\n<p>Focusing changing direction reactively (i.e., at the last possible second)</p>\n<p>Getting lower</p>\n<p>Improving your ability to see the field as you do these exercises</p>\n<p>Getting a partner to act as the offense</p>\n<p>Filming yourself to look for imbalances, inefficiencies, asymmetries, etc.</p>\n<p>Keep in mind that we’ll iterate on these throughout the season. It will be helpful to have as many players as possible familiar with these basic formats.</p>\n<h3>Drill 1: Slide Progression</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"1GW2SlIGWHgnrHNPz95MZV4Yk45zEjJi5\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 2: Focused Falling Leaf</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"1SR-oSGZfXt0YEei2pvOyt3YS5ZrG7qk-\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 3: Jumbo Hollywood Squares</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"1W6ivHvLy6AKedgCi_eOEGk9jOmfw6aeg\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 4a : Hip Control (Basics) / Drill 4b : Hip Control (Dictation)</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"1Y49jLkdf5lAbBKwkt9VWie4cL5F285n6\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"1ZMi4uD--6L_eJDejtYuIc_L4qlJW-Ar0\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 5 : Reactivity Box</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"1akrs-7RyWEwaLSa6_8bcKpDNC2X_aMsN\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 6 : Full Speed Stops and Dropsteps</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"1YMzE9jLCBoqhyuqMoY4YQ11bpVe2yTE0\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 7 : Marking Mechanics</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"12to-aUA9GsVn2iyNA85XdekgmUYgSVl4\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 8 : Reactive Shuffle 5 - 10 - 5</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"1omi9M1UR2p6qHyTVjtqvqT_xXz7JMbjF\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 9 : Peripheral Vision Deep Defense</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"1Gora2EBBcNyiNzaEoiDsCvxb_D6QsGkH\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>\n<h3>Drill 10 : Defending Clears (Working Hard Late)</h3>\n<div class=\"video\" data-drive=\"18NiBXWe90yT-bJunKF8Ta4xDRPMVAy0x\" data-label=\"Drill video\"></div>", "source": "club"}];
